Z||000004||Banzai||09-04-2001||12:09 PM||||I  didn't have access to a press and  I  am sandblasting and refinishing the entire  subframe and underbody so paint preservation wasn't a concern.  The project has otherwise gone very smoothly.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Nashco||09-04-2001||05:08 PM||||I just did my bushings this weekend, and had very good luck getting them out.  Rather than burn them out, or press them out, I did both!  I used a torch to heat the outside of the bushings (the metal sleeve) until a slight plume of smoke was coming off it, then I pushed it out.  This, I feel, was much easier than doing the other two methods singularly!  Also, when I tried just pressing the bushings out, the control arms looked like they were flexing; I wasn't very happy thinking about having deformed control arms after putting all that time and money into the new suspension.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
